<newsitem itemid="197560" id="root" date="1996-11-18" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Celsis H1 loss narrows as customers multiply.</title>
<headline>Celsis H1 loss narrows as customers multiply.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence, loss)	3.41		   vs 4.11</p>
<p> Pretax loss		2.6		    vs 2.9</p>
<p> Turnover		   4.2		    vs 1.7</p>
<p> Operating loss	   2.93		   vs 3.32</p>
<p> Interest received	0.23		   vs 0.33</p>
<p> Tax			  nil		    vs nil</p>
<p> Retained loss	    2.70		   vs 2.99</p>
<p>NOTE - Fast-growing microbial detection group Celsis International Plc said that as its revenue continues to rise and its partners underwrite more of its costs and market risk, it is moving towards profitability. A consensus among a group of share analysts sees Celsis reaching profit in the year to March 1998 and a company spokesman told Reuters it was &quot;not uncomfortable&quot; with that forecast.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
